{
  "name": "Send Slack briefs before Calendly calls with past.dev memory and OpenAI",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## A brief in Slack before every Calendly call\n\nFor sales and customer success people who walk into calls and want to know what was said last time, what is still open, and who else on the team talked to this person.\n\n### How it works\n- A new Calendly booking starts the workflow.\n- past.dev **Recall** returns what your company knows about the invitee and their company, with dates and sources.\n- If there is history, OpenAI writes a short brief from it. If there is none, the brief says so and does not invent one.\n- Slack gets the brief, and the booking is saved to past.dev for next time.\n\n### Setup\n1. Self-hosted n8n: open **Settings > Community Nodes**, select **Install** and enter `n8n-nodes-pastdotdev` (tested with 0.1.0 on n8n 2.47). [Installation guide](https://docs.n8n.io/integrations/community-nodes/installation/)\n2. Create a project API key in the [past.dev console](https://app.past.dev) and add it as a **Past Dev API** credential in each past.dev node.\n3. Add your Calendly, Slack and OpenAI credentials.\n4. In **Config**, set `slack_channel` (a channel ID or your own user ID) and `reader_identity`.\n\n### Customization\n- The brief is only as good as the memory. Fill it with the Gmail, Slack or Drive templates of past.dev, or with your CRM notes.\n- Change the brief format in **Write the brief**.\n- Use the Occurred From option of Recall to limit the brief to the last 90 days.\n",
        "height": 760,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "eaea39cc-209b-50e1-8e9b-5836c262421f",
      "name": "Sticky Note Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -800,
        -440
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## New booking\nConfig holds the Slack target and the reader identity.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 7
